    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen creating multiple cursors, if you then move down the file such that one or more cursors would be placed beyond the last line, those cursors are removed:\n\n[![asciicast](https://asciinema.org/a/LfchAzKz8m28fVzd.svg)](https://asciinema.org/a/LfchAzKz8m28fVzd)\n\nHere I create a few cursors then move them down such that multiple of them extend beyond the last line, and they end up being removed.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate the following buffer contents:\n\n```\nhello\nworld\nfoo\nbar\nbaz\ntest\n```\n\nMove the cursor to `h` on the first line, then enable visual block mode, move the cursor down a few lines and press `Q` to create multiple cursors. Next, move primary cursor down to the `test` line using `j`, then move it back up and observe the other cursors not coming back.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe cursors shouldn't be removed but merely \"hidden\" or \"ignored\" when performing certain operations, _or_ this should be documented. My apologies if I'm blind/stupid and this is already documented somewhere.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0a844adc133f732b236b1669c705d9aac888a5a0\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nnot relevant\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nFedora Workstation 45\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGNOME Ptyxis 50.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nGit",
