            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> > The cursors shouldn't be removed but merely \"hidden\" or \"ignored\" when performing certain operations\n> \n> Do you mean, you want the cursors to move off-screen, even though the primary cursor didn't?\n\nEssentially what I meant was that if after moving the cursor to the bottom you move it back up again, the cursors that \"clipped\" beyond the last line appear again.\n\nMy thinking here is that if you have follow mode enabled and you e.g. jump to the last line by accident, all your extra cursors are gone, which is not entirely intuitive.\n\nWith that said, I gave Helix a try to see what that does (just as a reference) and it seems to have the same behavior, so perhaps it's not as surprising/unintuitive as I thought :)\n\nEither way, thanks for #41812 😄 ",
